Review the results and make all changes at once before committing:

1. Bug: guidanceApplied causes the guidance to only be added on the first run. pi rebuilds the system prompt on every run (agent-session.ts's _runAgentPrompt clears _systemPromptOverride in the finally block), so from the second turn onward there's no guidance. Change it so that every before_agent_start returns a systemPrompt with the guidance appended, and only the log 'vehicle guidance applied chars=N' is emitted once per process. Also, if event.systemPrompt already ends with this guidance text, don't append it again.
2. Revert the swap of the catalog/transport assignment order in the McpCatalogBridge constructor (unrelated to this task). Keeping transport as a readonly public field is fine.
3. Add all tests required by handoff-97:
   - device-mcp: without guidance, initialize output is byte-for-byte identical to the original; with guidance, result.instructions equals this text.
   - progressive-tools:
     - With instructions, two consecutive before_agent_start calls both return a system prompt ending with '\n'+instructions, and the log is emitted only once;
     - Without instructions, it doesn't return or modify the system prompt;
     - decide (preexpand) requests don't include the guidance;
     - HttpMcpTransport can parse instructions from the initialize result.
4. Gates:
   - cd rust && cargo test -p device-mcp, test count must be greater than 8;
   - cd pi_extensions/progressive-tools && npm test, test count must be greater than 99;
   - No clippy warnings on changed files.
5. Commit with the trailer 'Co-Authored-By: gpt-6-luna (codex) <noreply@openai.com>'. Don't use git commit -a, don't commit CLAUDE.md. Final git status --short should only show CLAUDE.md.
